Chapter 1 said the stretching of space wound the clock, and left a hot star in a cold sky. This is where the winding gets spent.

<!-- AI-assisted diagram, 2026-11-15: solar energy balance and photon-number/entropy distinction. -->
![Sunlight and outgoing heat carry roughly the same energy at approximate balance, but in different numbers of photons. Cooler thermal radiation spreads that energy among many more photons and exports more entropy. This thermal estimate excludes reflected sunlight; it does not trace individual photons through a food chain.](assets/02-chapter/sunlight-entropy.svg){#fig-c2-sunlight-entropy width=95%}

How much inherited detail can persist depends on how well it is copied and repaired.

<!-- AI-assisted diagram, 2026-11-15: illustrative favored-sequence model, not a universal genome-size bound. -->
![Copying can consume a reproductive advantage. Here the favored sequence reproduces twice as fast, but only a fraction Q of its copies remain faithful. Once 2Q falls below the background rate of one, that sequence cannot maintain its advantage in this simple model. The curve assumes independent copying errors and negligible back mutation.](assets/02-chapter/copying-fidelity.svg){#fig-c2-copying-fidelity width=90%}
